{"name":"Roasted Sesame","hex":"#fec36b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roasted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by roasting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of roast"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roasted"},{"term":"sesame","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tropical Asian plant (Sesamum indicum) bearing small flat seeds used as food and as a source of oil.","The seed of this plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sesame"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roasting","blocks":[{"text":"Roasting is a cooking method that uses dry heat where hot air covers the food, cooking it evenly on all sides with temperatures of at least 150 °C (300 °F) from an open flame, oven, or other heat source. Roasting can enhance the flavor through caramelization and Maillard browning on the surface of the food. Roasting uses indirect, diffused heat, and is suitable for slower cooking of meat in a larger, whole piece. Meats and most root and bulb vegetables can be roasted. Any piece of meat, especially red meat, that has been cooked in this fashion is called a roast. Meats and vegetables prepared in this way are described as \"roasted\", e.g., roasted chicken or roasted squash."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Roast_Pig_1.JPG/330px-Roast_Pig_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roasting"},{"title":"Sesame","blocks":[{"text":"Sesame is a plant in the genus Sesamum, also called benne. Numerous wild relatives occur in Africa and a smaller number in India. It is widely naturalized in tropical regions around the world and is cultivated for its edible seeds, which grow in pods. World production in 2024 was 6.7 million tonnes, with India, Myanmar, and Sudan as the largest producers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Sesamum_indicum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-129.jpg/330px-Sesamum_indicum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-129.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sesame"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/500px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/1280px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/500px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tudor style roasting meat on a spit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg/500px-Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg/500px-Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Sunday roast consisting of roast beef, potatoes, vegetables, and Yorkshire pudding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Max%27s_Roasted_Chicken_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg/500px-Max%27s_Roasted_Chicken_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Max%27s_Roasted_Chicken_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg/1280px-Max%2